And then he also has a scene with Ryan where he is saying that it's just another kind of
然后他还有一场和瑞安的戏，他说这又是一个

464
00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:52.750
boring day.
无聊的日子。

465
00:21:53.170 --> 00:21:54.210
Nothing's going to happen.
什么都不会发生。

466
00:21:54.690 --> 00:22:00.210
And he's talking about how on Big Brother, they tackle really important things, you know,
他说《老大哥》节目每周都会处理一些非常重要的事情，

467
00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:01.130
every week.
你知道的。

468
00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:02.570
But I guess that's not real life.
但我想那不是现实生活。

469
00:22:02.570 --> 00:22:07.210
And he, you can tell that Michael wants to feel accomplished in this day.
你能看出迈克尔想在这一天里感到有所成就。

470
00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:09.330
He wants to feel like he made a difference.
他想感觉自己做出了改变。

471
00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:16.950
Well, I think that deleted scene is a great way that we motivate Michael's whole desire
嗯，我觉得那个删减片段很好地解释了迈克尔为什么渴望

472
00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:20.330
to take over the conflict resolution in the office for the day.
在这一天接手办公室的冲突调解工作。

473
00:22:20.450 --> 00:22:26.430
Because now in the next scene, Ryan is in Michael's office and he hears Oscar yelling
因为紧接着下一场戏，瑞安在迈克尔办公室里，他听到奥斯卡在

474
00:22:26.430 --> 00:22:27.630
from the conference room.
会议室里大喊大叫。

475
00:22:27.790 --> 00:22:29.390
Oscar is going off.
奥斯卡发火了。

476
00:22:29.390 --> 00:22:35.570
I know the beginning of that scene, the stuff that they're overhearing Oscar saying, Oscar's
我知道那场戏的开头，他们偷听到的奥斯卡说的话，是奥斯卡

477
00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:38.770
improvising because they were like, OK, just make a big fuss.
即兴发挥的，因为当时导演说，好吧，你就闹大点。

478
00:22:39.050 --> 00:22:42.330
They'll overhear it and it will cause them to leave Michael's office.
他们会听到动静，然后离开迈克尔的办公室。

479
00:22:42.490 --> 00:22:42.630
Right.
没错。

480
00:22:42.770 --> 00:22:44.390
Go see what the hubbub is about.
去看看发生了什么事。

481
00:22:44.890 --> 00:22:45.030
Yeah.
是啊。

482
00:22:45.210 --> 00:22:47.510
And Oscar's a very funny improviser.
奥斯卡是个非常有趣的即兴表演者。

483
00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:49.810
And he got he got to have some fun in this episode.
他在这一集里玩得很开心。

484
00:22:50.070 --> 00:22:52.330
Oh, all those lines are amazing.
噢，那些台词真是太棒了。

485
00:22:52.330 --> 00:22:59.810
Michael goes into the conference room and he sees Oscar is with Toby and he is ranting about
迈克尔走进会议室，看到奥斯卡和托比在一起，他正在抱怨

486
00:22:59.810 --> 00:23:06.690
Angela's baby jazz poster that Toby gave her in the Secret Santa exchange at Christmas.
安吉拉那张托比在圣诞节秘密圣诞老人交换礼物时送给她的爵士乐宝宝海报。

487
00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:07.350
Yes.
是的。

488
00:23:07.750 --> 00:23:12.050
She has hung it in accounting and Oscar doesn't want to look at it anymore.
她把它挂在会计部，奥斯卡不想再看到了。

489
00:23:13.070 --> 00:23:14.510
He's furious.
他气疯了。

490
00:23:14.510 --> 00:23:18.990
And Toby's like, listen, you normally wouldn't hear this ranting.
托比说，听着，平时你不会听到这种抱怨的。

491
00:23:19.310 --> 00:23:23.210
Normally we do it in the break room, but they're doing the security badge photos in there.
平时我们是在休息室里谈的，但那里正在拍安保胸牌照片。

492
00:23:23.310 --> 00:23:24.690
So we're doing it in here instead.
所以我们才改到这里来。

493
00:23:25.010 --> 00:23:26.870
And this is Michael's opportunity.
这就是迈克尔的机会。

494
00:23:27.150 --> 00:23:28.710
He has found his purpose.
他找到了自己的人生目标。

495
00:23:29.070 --> 00:23:30.370
And this is it.
就是这个。

496
00:23:30.590 --> 00:23:31.750
He's so excited.
他太兴奋了。

497
00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.250
He decides he's going to resolve this conflict.
他决定要解决这场冲突。

498
00:23:35.250 --> 00:23:38.670
So he calls Angela and Oscar into the conference room and Pam.
于是他把安吉拉、奥斯卡和帕姆叫进了会议室。

499
00:23:39.150 --> 00:23:41.290
Apparently, Pam had to attend.
显然，帕姆也得参加。

500
00:23:41.590 --> 00:23:44.090
Pam gets pulled into so many things with Michael.
帕姆总是被卷进迈克尔的各种破事里。

501
00:23:44.550 --> 00:23:47.210
It's like he needs her to document it in some way.
就好像他需要她以某种方式记录下来一样。

502
00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:47.810
I don't know.
我不知道。

503
00:23:47.990 --> 00:23:49.550
But I'm not writing anything down.
但我什么都没写。

504
00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:50.210
No, you know.
不，你知道的。

505
00:23:50.290 --> 00:23:52.150
And you hardly ever are.
而且你几乎从不写什么。

506
00:23:52.470 --> 00:23:54.350
No, it's so true.
不，这太对了。

507
00:23:54.550 --> 00:23:55.850
He just likes to feel important.
他只是喜欢那种重要感。

508
00:23:55.990 --> 00:23:57.870
He likes to feel like he has a personal assistant.
他喜欢那种有私人助理的感觉。

509
00:23:58.350 --> 00:23:58.750
Yes.
没错。

510
00:23:58.910 --> 00:24:05.610
I like how quickly he produced this poster board that says communicate this binder.
我喜欢他拿出那块写着“沟通”的展示板的速度，还有那个活页夹。

511
00:24:05.850 --> 00:24:06.570
He's had this.
他一直都有这个。

512
00:24:06.730 --> 00:24:07.650
He has been waiting.
他一直在等这一刻。

513
00:24:07.950 --> 00:24:08.930
He has had this.
他一直留着这个。

514
00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:10.150
He's ready to go.
他随时准备着。

515
00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:11.590
But you know what I think, Angela?
但你知道我在想什么吗，安吉拉？

516
00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:17.750
Well, I think corporate gave him this binder a long time ago to look through and study.
嗯，我觉得公司很久以前就给了他这个活页夹让他研究学习。

517
00:24:17.890 --> 00:24:20.450
And he's never cracked it open until now.
但他直到现在才翻开它。

518
00:24:20.570 --> 00:24:20.870
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

519
00:24:20.970 --> 00:24:23.770
He was like, I can't be bothered with this binder.
他当时的态度就是，我才懒得管这个活页夹呢。

520
00:24:23.970 --> 00:24:26.670
And now suddenly he's ripped it off the shelf.
结果现在他突然把它从架子上拿下来了。

521
00:24:26.670 --> 00:24:30.270
We had a fan question from Aiden Magia.
我们收到了艾登·马吉亚的一个粉丝提问。

522
00:24:30.570 --> 00:24:34.790
You know, we go through the different styles of conflict resolution.
你知道，我们讨论过不同的冲突解决方式。

523
00:24:35.630 --> 00:24:41.970
And Aiden wanted to know, did it ever mention in the script what the number two and number
艾登想知道，剧本里有没有提到五种冲突解决方式中，第二种和第三种

524
00:24:41.970 --> 00:24:46.590
three resolutions were in the five different styles of conflict?
分别是什么？

525
00:24:46.590 --> 00:24:49.490
I don't know, but I know what the five are.
我不知道，但我知道那五种是什么。

526
00:24:49.710 --> 00:24:54.270
The only one that's referred to in the script that isn't listed in this scene is compromise.
剧本里提到过但这一幕没列出来的只有“妥协”。

527
00:24:54.710 --> 00:25:05.570
So the five types of conflict resolution are lose-lose, win-lose, compromise, win-win, and win-win-win.
所以五种冲突解决方式是：双输、赢输、妥协、双赢，以及三赢。

528
00:25:06.430 --> 00:25:09.930
So they're really, Michael's really keyed in on a win-win-win.
所以迈克尔真的非常执着于“三赢”。

529
00:25:11.110 --> 00:25:12.670
Because then even he wins.
因为那样连他自己也能赢。

530
00:25:12.990 --> 00:25:13.150
Yes.
是的。

531
00:25:13.210 --> 00:25:14.910
We know lose-lose is number one.
我们知道第一种是双输。

532
00:25:15.010 --> 00:25:17.810
And then Angela just wants him to just skip to win-win.
然后安吉拉只想让他直接跳到双赢。

533
00:25:17.930 --> 00:25:19.050
And he goes, that's number four.
但他却说，那是第四种。

534
00:25:19.190 --> 00:25:24.470
But then I love Steve's performance so much when he starts to read number five.
但我太喜欢史蒂夫在读第五种时的表演了。

535
00:25:24.690 --> 00:25:26.790
And here's the thing that Steve is doing.
史蒂夫在这里的处理方式是这样的。

536
00:25:27.230 --> 00:25:33.090
He's reading something and making it look like he's never read it before and that he's getting surprised as he reads it.
他读着东西，表现得好像他以前从没读过一样，读的时候还表现出很惊讶的样子。

537
00:25:33.090 --> 00:25:33.350
Yes.
没错。

538
00:25:33.470 --> 00:25:36.910
Even though you and I both know he knew those lines backwards and forwards.
尽管你我都清楚他早就把那些台词背得滚瓜烂熟了。

539
00:25:36.910 --> 00:25:40.830
So he's like, oh, number five, win-win-win.
所以他表现得像，哦，第五种，三赢。

540
00:25:40.970 --> 00:25:41.710
Oh, I win!
哦，我赢了！

541
00:25:41.890 --> 00:25:44.330
I win, too, because I resolved it.
我也赢了，因为我解决了问题。

542
00:25:44.650 --> 00:25:46.810
And it's just, he's so good.
他真的太棒了。

543
00:25:46.810 --> 00:25:55.430
Just in that very, like, small moment, you see how great he is at finessing all of these little moments.
就在那短短的一瞬间，你就能看出他处理这些小细节的能力有多强。

544
00:25:55.550 --> 00:25:56.110
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

545
00:25:56.170 --> 00:25:59.690
They should play that in acting schools as an example of moment of discovery.
表演学校应该把这段当作“发现时刻”的范例来播放。

546
00:25:59.910 --> 00:26:00.130
All right.
好的。

547
00:26:00.190 --> 00:26:04.690
So at four minutes, 32 seconds, they go over to, quote, look at the disputed poster.
在4分32秒时，他们走过去，“查看”那张有争议的海报。

548
00:26:04.950 --> 00:26:06.750
Michael wants them to express their feelings.
迈克尔想让他们表达自己的感受。

549
00:26:06.910 --> 00:26:19.250
And I say that the poster makes me happy because it makes me feel like the babies are the real artists, that God has a funny sense of humor.
我说那张海报让我很高兴，因为它让我觉得婴儿才是真正的艺术家，上帝真有幽默感。

550
00:26:19.470 --> 00:26:23.430
And Oscar, at five minutes, two seconds, just goes off.
而在5分02秒，奥斯卡突然爆发了。

551
00:26:23.550 --> 00:26:25.330
And he has this rant.
他当时有一段长篇大论。

552
00:26:25.530 --> 00:26:27.710
It was so fun to do this with Oscar.
能和奥斯卡一起拍这段戏太有趣了。

553
00:26:27.870 --> 00:26:29.950
I have known him for so long.
我认识他很久了。

554
00:26:29.950 --> 00:26:32.450
We performed together in sketch comedy.
我们以前一起演过小品喜剧。

555
00:26:32.570 --> 00:26:37.070
So I knew when they told him he could uncork what that meant.
所以我知道当他们告诉他可以畅所欲言时，那意味着什么。

556
00:26:37.070 --> 00:26:41.950
And it was just a delight for me when he was like, you know what?
当他说出那番话时，我真的觉得特别开心，你知道吗？

557
00:26:42.090 --> 00:26:43.030
It's kitsch.
那是媚俗。

558
00:26:43.030 --> 00:26:44.270
It's the opposite of art.
那是艺术的对立面。

559
00:26:44.450 --> 00:26:45.350
It destroys art.
它摧毁艺术。

560
00:26:45.470 --> 00:26:46.910
It destroys souls.
它摧毁灵魂。

561
00:26:47.610 --> 00:26:49.030
It just goes off.
他简直停不下来。

562
00:26:49.070 --> 00:26:52.070
Was that improvised or scripted, Angela, or a mixture?
安吉拉，那段是即兴发挥还是照着剧本演的，或者是两者都有？

563
00:26:53.050 --> 00:26:54.190
It was a mixture.
两者都有。

564
00:26:54.370 --> 00:26:54.850
It was a mixture.
两者都有。

565
00:26:54.990 --> 00:26:56.950
And I think that was mostly scripted.
我觉得大部分是剧本里的。

566
00:26:57.030 --> 00:27:02.890
But his stuff with Paul, with Toby in the conference room at the top of that scene was improvised.
但他在那场戏开头和保罗，也就是托比在会议室里的互动是即兴的。

567
00:27:03.030 --> 00:27:06.670
But Oscar is just so funny in this.
不过奥斯卡在这段里真的太搞笑了。

568
00:27:06.670 --> 00:27:09.290
And I just remember it was hard to keep a straight face.
我记得当时很难忍住不笑。

569
00:27:09.470 --> 00:27:10.010
I remember that.
我记得那次。

570
00:27:10.170 --> 00:27:13.310
I had you to my right and Oscar to my left.
你坐在我右边，奥斯卡坐在我左边。

571
00:27:13.430 --> 00:27:14.430
It was very hard.
真的很难。

572
00:27:14.630 --> 00:27:17.450
It was very hard for me because Pam doesn't have any lines.
对我来说特别难，因为帕姆在那段戏里没有台词。

573
00:27:17.450 --> 00:27:21.310
And my direction was that I was not to react.
导演给我的要求是不能有任何反应。

574
00:27:22.070 --> 00:27:25.590
I was to remain very neutral as possible.
我必须尽可能保持中立。

575
00:27:25.830 --> 00:27:28.790
And so that was difficult to be neutral.
所以要保持中立真的很难。

576
00:27:29.410 --> 00:27:30.010
All right.
好吧。

577
00:27:30.010 --> 00:27:32.270
Well, we had a fan question from Zoe Kennedy.
我们收到了一个来自佐伊·肯尼迪的粉丝提问。

578
00:27:33.090 --> 00:27:36.430
What do you guys think a win-win-win solution?
你们觉得什么样的方案才算得上是“三赢”？

579
00:27:36.670 --> 00:27:40.410
To Oscar and Angela's dispute with the baby poster would be.
能解决奥斯卡和安吉拉关于婴儿海报的争端。

580
00:27:40.570 --> 00:27:48.610
Because, you know, Michael's win-win-win solution is that Oscar will turn the baby poster into a t-shirt.
因为迈克尔提出的“三赢”方案是让奥斯卡把婴儿海报做成T恤。

581
00:27:48.810 --> 00:27:49.390
T-shirt.
T恤。

582
00:27:49.690 --> 00:27:52.270
That he has to wear because then he won't see it.
他必须穿上它，这样他就看不见海报了。

583
00:27:52.350 --> 00:27:53.910
But Angela will see it all the time.
但安吉拉会一直看到它。

584
00:27:55.630 --> 00:27:56.070
Yes.
没错。

585
00:27:56.270 --> 00:27:58.110
And neither of them like that.
而且他们俩都不喜欢这样。

586
00:27:58.390 --> 00:27:58.870
They're like, eh.
他们都觉得，呃。

587
00:27:58.870 --> 00:27:59.750
Neither of them like that.
他们俩都不喜欢。

588
00:27:59.930 --> 00:28:02.250
So what would you make it be, Ang?
那么安吉拉，你会怎么解决呢？

589
00:28:02.310 --> 00:28:03.470
What's your win-win-win?
你的“三赢”方案是什么？

590
00:28:03.610 --> 00:28:06.470
I would say that you could have personal items that could fit on your desk.
我会说，你可以放一些能摆在桌子上的个人物品。

591
00:28:06.670 --> 00:28:09.190
And as long as they weren't offensive, they could stay on your desk.
只要不冒犯他人，就可以留在桌子上。

592
00:28:09.350 --> 00:28:10.090
I like that.
我喜欢这个主意。

593
00:28:10.170 --> 00:28:13.450
You shrink it down to, like, no bigger than an 8x10.
你把它缩小到不超过8x10英寸的大小。

594
00:28:13.630 --> 00:28:15.290
And then she could put it on her desk.
然后她就可以把它放在自己的桌子上了。

595
00:28:15.310 --> 00:28:16.950
And that would be my win-win-win.
这就是我的“三赢”方案。

596
00:28:17.730 --> 00:28:20.450
Angela, that is a great solution.
安吉拉，这真是个好主意。

597
00:28:22.750 --> 00:28:23.310
Thank you.
谢谢。

598
00:28:23.310 --> 00:28:27.570
You set a new rule that personal items can be no larger than 8x10.
你定下了一条新规，个人物品不得超过8x10英寸。

599
00:28:28.610 --> 00:28:29.870
That's it, everyone.
就是这样，各位。

600
00:28:30.270 --> 00:28:31.370
You heard it here firSt.
你们在这里第一时间听到了。

601
00:28:31.370 --> 00:28:32.310
You're welcome, corporate America.
不客气，美国企业界。

602
00:28:32.310 --> 00:28:33.050
You heard it here.
你们都听到了。

603
00:28:33.850 --> 00:28:34.430
All right.
好的。

604
00:28:34.610 --> 00:28:35.330
So moving on.
那么继续。

605
00:28:35.470 --> 00:28:36.170
What is next?
接下来是什么？

606
00:28:36.790 --> 00:28:41.090
So, Angela, we got a really cool fan question about this scene from Maricela Cabuto.
安吉拉，我们收到一个来自玛丽塞拉·卡布托的非常棒的粉丝提问，关于这个场景的。

607
00:28:41.590 --> 00:28:46.490
And I loved it so much, I reached out and I asked her if she would send me a recording
我太喜欢这个问题了，所以我联系了她，问她愿不愿意录一段音

608
00:28:46.490 --> 00:28:47.850
of her asking the question.
发给我，由她亲自提问。

609
00:28:47.970 --> 00:28:48.590
So here it goes.
所以，请听。

610
00:28:48.590 --> 00:28:53.990
When Michael is trying to solve the Angela-Oskar dispute, they are all standing in the accounting
当迈克尔试图解决安吉拉和奥斯卡的纠纷时，他们都站在会计部

611
00:28:53.990 --> 00:28:54.650
area.
区域。

612
00:28:54.830 --> 00:29:00.650
On a column behind Michael, there is a certificate of participation for a Mark Christie.
在迈克尔身后的一根柱子上，有一张马克·克里斯蒂的参与证书。

613
00:29:01.210 --> 00:29:02.190
Who is that?
那是谁？

614
00:29:02.650 --> 00:29:06.610
I was so excited to get this question, Angela.
安吉拉，我收到这个问题时太兴奋了。

615
00:29:06.610 --> 00:29:10.090
So this moment happens at 4 minutes 32 seconds.
这一幕发生在4分32秒。

616
00:29:10.330 --> 00:29:17.990
And right next to Steve's head on this pillar, reception is behind the pillar, you can see
就在史蒂夫头旁边的柱子上，前台就在柱子后面，你可以看到

617
00:29:17.990 --> 00:29:19.150
this plaque.
这块牌匾。

618
00:29:19.390 --> 00:29:21.150
It's exactly what Maricela described.
正是玛丽塞拉所描述的那样。

619
00:29:21.150 --> 00:29:25.190
It is a certificate of participation for Mark Christie.
那确实是一张马克·克里斯蒂的参与证书。

620
00:29:25.770 --> 00:29:28.330
This is one of my favorite things about our set.
这是我最喜欢我们片场的细节之一。

621
00:29:28.510 --> 00:29:28.690
Okay.
好的。

622
00:29:28.850 --> 00:29:33.590
So Mark was the best boy grip and the key grip for seasons one through three on The Office.
马克是《办公室》第一到第三季的最佳灯光助理和灯光师。

623
00:29:33.590 --> 00:29:41.610
And it's the art department that is ultimately responsible for any kind of card, sign, certificate,
美术部门最终负责所有为剧集专门制作的卡片、标志、证书

624
00:29:41.610 --> 00:29:45.230
or logo that's created specifically for the show.
或徽标。

625
00:29:45.390 --> 00:29:51.510
So our art department created the Dunder Mifflin logo and they created all of the little plaques
所以我们的美术部门制作了邓德·米夫林的徽标，也制作了所有挂在办公室里的

626
00:29:51.510 --> 00:29:54.390
and signs and certificates that hang around the office.
小牌匾、标志和证书。

627
00:29:54.570 --> 00:30:01.370
And in an effort to give just like a fun personal touch, they would include the names of real crew
为了增添一点有趣的个人色彩，他们会把真实剧组人员的

628
00:30:01.370 --> 00:30:01.790
members.
名字放上去。

629
00:30:01.790 --> 00:30:02.570
Yes.
没错。

630
00:30:02.790 --> 00:30:07.690
So for example, we also had a Salesman of the Year and a Humanitarian of the Year plaque.
比如，我们还有“年度销售员”和“年度人道主义者”的牌匾。

631
00:30:07.910 --> 00:30:11.270
And those plaques featured our crew member names as well.
那些牌匾上也印着我们剧组成员的名字。

632
00:30:11.450 --> 00:30:13.470
But really, you can see them everywhere.
其实，你到处都能看到它们。

633
00:30:13.610 --> 00:30:15.590
You'll start to notice them as you watch episodes.
当你观看剧集时，你会开始注意到它们。

634
00:30:15.590 --> 00:30:16.350
I do now.
我现在会了。

635
00:30:16.510 --> 00:30:17.310
I look for them.
我会特意去找它们。

636
00:30:17.470 --> 00:30:17.590
Yeah.
是啊。

637
00:30:17.690 --> 00:30:20.070
There are tons that are just sprinkled throughout the whole office.
整个办公室里到处都散布着很多这样的东西。

638
00:30:20.270 --> 00:30:21.970
Well, let me tell you what my favorite one is.
好吧，让我告诉你们我最喜欢哪一个。

639
00:30:22.230 --> 00:30:22.370
Okay.
好的。

640
00:30:22.550 --> 00:30:22.770
Okay.
好的。

641
00:30:22.770 --> 00:30:28.410
So my favorite one involves our first AD, Kelly Cantley.
我最喜欢的一个涉及我们的第一副导演凯莉·坎特利。

642
00:30:28.590 --> 00:30:29.930
You guys might remember her.
你们可能还记得她。

643
00:30:29.930 --> 00:30:33.790
Kelly, her job is keeping all of the actors on schedule.
凯莉的工作是确保所有演员按进度表行事。

644
00:30:34.090 --> 00:30:37.630
She makes sure that we arrive for our scenes when we're supposed to.
她确保我们按时到达拍摄现场。

645
00:30:37.770 --> 00:30:41.130
And she is also the one who would run our safety meetings.
她也是负责主持安全会议的人。

646
00:30:41.290 --> 00:30:41.530
Yes.
是的。

647
00:30:41.750 --> 00:30:46.250
So Kelly Cantley was safety meeting, lit candle on set.
所以凯莉·坎特利主持安全会议，片场点蜡烛。

648
00:30:46.450 --> 00:30:47.490
That's Kelly Cantley.
那就是凯莉·坎特利。

649
00:30:47.490 --> 00:30:50.750
We have a pair of scissors in someone's hand.
我们有人手里拿着剪刀。

650
00:30:51.110 --> 00:30:51.770
Safety meeting.
安全会议。

651
00:30:52.050 --> 00:30:52.670
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是这样。

652
00:30:52.910 --> 00:30:53.250
Exactly.
确实。

653
00:30:53.750 --> 00:30:57.490
But Kelly really had to keep the whole production on time.
但凯莉确实得保证整个制作过程准时进行。

654
00:30:57.910 --> 00:31:03.730
Everything happening on the set, all of us working together and getting our day done,
片场发生的一切，我们所有人通力合作，按时完成当天的拍摄任务，

655
00:31:03.910 --> 00:31:04.570
making our day.
完成当天的进度。

656
00:31:04.570 --> 00:31:10.610
She's by far one of the most important elements to running the show, for sure.
毫无疑问，她是维持节目运作最重要的成员之一。

657
00:31:10.870 --> 00:31:18.110
Well, I guess that Kelly had gone around and looked at all the plaques and she noticed
嗯，我猜凯莉当时到处转了转，看了所有的牌匾，然后她注意到

658
00:31:18.110 --> 00:31:20.970
that her name was not on any of them.
上面都没有她的名字。

659
00:31:22.370 --> 00:31:24.850
I can kind of picture Kelly doing that, actually.
说实话，我能想象出凯莉当时的样子。

660
00:31:25.170 --> 00:31:31.170
She spent a couple of days sort of doing this bit where she was all like, oh, I see.
她花了好几天时间，演了一出戏，大概就是那种，哦，我明白了。

661
00:31:32.010 --> 00:31:33.510
No, no, Kelly, Kelly.
不，不，凯莉，凯莉。

662
00:31:33.690 --> 00:31:34.890
There's my name is on any plaque.
我的名字根本不在任何牌匾上。

663
00:31:34.890 --> 00:31:35.770
It was very funny.
那真的很有趣。

664
00:31:36.250 --> 00:31:41.130
And then all of a sudden, one day, a new plaque showed up.
然后突然有一天，出现了一块新的牌匾。

665
00:31:41.630 --> 00:31:45.090
It's on the pole over by Stanley's desk.
就在斯坦利办公桌旁边的柱子上。

666
00:31:45.090 --> 00:31:46.710
And here's what it said.
上面是这么写的。

667
00:31:47.170 --> 00:31:55.890
It said, whereas it came to our attention that Kelly Cantley was whining, that a lowly
上面写着，鉴于我们注意到凯莉·坎特利在抱怨，说一个低微的

668
00:31:55.890 --> 00:31:59.070
second assistant director had a plaque with her name on it.
第二助理导演都有写着她名字的牌匾。

669
00:31:59.150 --> 00:32:05.310
And whereas Kelly Cantley made a comment on the air regarding that fact, we have decided
鉴于凯莉·坎特利在节目中就此事发表了评论，我们决定

670
00:32:05.310 --> 00:32:08.970
to give her this certificate because we love her.
给她颁发这个证书，因为我们爱她。

671
00:32:10.350 --> 00:32:12.150
Isn't that so fun?
这难道不有趣吗？

672
00:32:12.150 --> 00:32:15.650
And so and then they just waited for her to notice it.
然后他们就等着她发现它。

673
00:32:15.750 --> 00:32:18.330
And then it stayed there for the rest of the run of the show.
它就在那里一直留到了剧集结束。

674
00:32:18.490 --> 00:32:20.970
So, guys, something fun to do.
所以，伙计们，这事儿挺好玩的。

675
00:32:21.190 --> 00:32:26.930
You can go through, try to hit pause whenever you see these certificates and you can see
你们可以试着在看到这些证书时按下暂停，这样就能看到

676
00:32:26.930 --> 00:32:28.650
some names of our crew members.
我们一些剧组成员的名字了。

677
00:32:28.650 --> 00:32:31.410
I think it's just a really, really great way to honor them.
我觉得这真的是一种非常非常棒的致敬方式。

678
00:32:31.530 --> 00:32:35.530
And this is actually a very popular thing that happens on sets.
而且这实际上在片场是很常见的事情。

679
00:32:36.030 --> 00:32:36.430
Yes.
是的。

680
00:32:36.790 --> 00:32:37.110
All right.
好的。

681
00:32:37.190 --> 00:32:38.090
I love that question.
我很喜欢这个问题。

682
00:32:38.090 --> 00:32:41.130
I love hearing the behind the scenes of our crew.
我很喜欢听关于我们剧组的幕后故事。

683
00:32:41.130 --> 00:32:47.130
Um, but Jenna, it's time to get into the save the date.
嗯，不过珍娜，是时候聊聊“预留日期”卡片了。

684
00:32:47.610 --> 00:32:47.970
Yes.
好的。

685
00:32:48.210 --> 00:32:49.890
Six minutes, 28 seconds.
6分28秒。

686
00:32:49.890 --> 00:32:52.330
We get a real bird's eye view of this.
我们能从上帝视角看这一幕。

687
00:32:52.710 --> 00:32:59.150
Well, Pam has broken down and is giving Angela a save the date hand delivered.
帕姆终于妥协了，亲自把“预留日期”卡片送给了安吉拉。

688
00:32:59.430 --> 00:33:02.210
We have a fan question from Miss Lavender Darling.
我们有一个来自拉文德·达林小姐的粉丝提问。

689
00:33:02.750 --> 00:33:07.550
She said, Pam's save the date invitations say place TBA.
她说，帕姆的“预留日期”邀请函上写着地点待定。

690
00:33:08.850 --> 00:33:14.590
Why did she bother making a save the date with a location TB?
为什么她还要费心制作一张地点待定的“预留日期”卡片呢？

691
00:33:15.110 --> 00:33:15.590
TBD.
是待定。

692
00:33:15.950 --> 00:33:17.350
When I looked at the save the date.
当我看到那张“预留日期”卡片时。

693
00:33:17.530 --> 00:33:19.250
OK, first of all, Angela's throwing shade.
好吧，首先，安吉拉在阴阳怪气。

694
00:33:19.390 --> 00:33:21.030
She's like, it's hand delivered, but it's OK.
她就像是说，虽然是亲手送的，但也还行吧。

695
00:33:21.190 --> 00:33:22.470
But it's also not my taste.
但那也不是我的品味。

696
00:33:22.690 --> 00:33:24.530
So she's throwing a lot of shade.
所以她一直在冷嘲热讽。

697
00:33:24.530 --> 00:33:31.410
But I screen grabbed the save the date and it says save the date and then written in
但我截屏了那张“预留日期”卡片，上面写着“预留日期”，然后是手写的

698
00:33:31.410 --> 00:33:31.710
hand.
内容。

699
00:33:31.910 --> 00:33:34.930
So, you know, it's printed, but then you've got to fill in everything by hand.
所以，你知道，它是印刷的，但你得把所有信息都手写填上去。

700
00:33:34.930 --> 00:33:38.270
It says for the wedding, Pam Beasley to Roy Anderson.
上面写着婚礼，帕姆·比斯利嫁给罗伊·安德森。

701
00:33:38.510 --> 00:33:39.310
Date June 10th.
日期是6月10日。

702
00:33:39.430 --> 00:33:40.770
Place to be determined.
地点待定。

703
00:33:41.090 --> 00:33:43.770
The save the date gives us nothing.
这张“预留日期”卡片什么信息都没给我们。

704
00:33:44.790 --> 00:33:51.030
Everyone in the office knew it was going to be June 10th because Roy announced it drunkenly
办公室里每个人都知道是6月10日，因为罗伊在酒会上喝醉了之后宣布的，

705
00:33:51.030 --> 00:33:51.970
on booze cruise.
就在那次游轮派对上。

706
00:33:52.710 --> 00:33:54.730
We know it's between the two of you.
我们知道这事儿就在你们俩之间。

707
00:33:55.030 --> 00:33:56.890
This save the date is pointless.
这张“预留日期”卡片毫无意义。

708
00:33:57.470 --> 00:33:57.630
Yeah.
没错。

709
00:33:57.810 --> 00:33:58.830
It's a waste of time.
简直是浪费时间。

710
00:33:59.010 --> 00:34:00.050
It's a waste of money.
简直是浪费钱。

711
00:34:00.330 --> 00:34:01.230
Kind of like their wedding.
就像他们的婚礼一样。

712
00:34:01.430 --> 00:34:02.650
Oh, my God.
天哪。

713
00:34:02.770 --> 00:34:05.150
Can I get an Angela Sass, please?
能给我来一份“安吉拉式吐槽”吗？

714
00:34:05.450 --> 00:34:05.500
I didn't.
我没做。

715
00:34:05.500 --> 00:34:05.550
I did.
我做了。

716
00:34:05.870 --> 00:34:06.110
Sam.
萨姆。

717
00:34:06.350 --> 00:34:07.430
Angela Sass.
安吉拉式吐槽。

718
00:34:07.610 --> 00:34:08.310
There it is.
这就对了。

719
00:34:08.470 --> 00:34:09.910
I agree with you, Angela.
我同意你的看法，安吉拉。

720
00:34:09.910 --> 00:34:18.110
I think that these rather lame, handwritten save the dates are a waste of time.
我觉得这些手写的、相当蹩脚的“预留日期”卡片就是在浪费时间。

721
00:34:18.310 --> 00:34:22.670
Did you do save the dates for your wedding or did you just send an invitation?
你们结婚时发了“预留日期”卡片，还是只发了请柬？

722
00:34:23.070 --> 00:34:26.830
Well, you know, I did just an email save the date.
嗯，你知道的，我当时只是发了封电子邮件来预留日期。

723
00:34:27.050 --> 00:34:27.470
Yeah.
是啊。

724
00:34:27.810 --> 00:34:28.770
I did an email.
我发的是邮件。

725
00:34:28.850 --> 00:34:29.010
Yeah.
没错。

726
00:34:29.110 --> 00:34:30.710
That's a little bit where we are now.
我们现在差不多就是这种情况。

727
00:34:30.930 --> 00:34:38.410
I think I'll say I did a save the date, a hard copy save the date thing, I think.
我想我会说我发了“预留日期”卡片，那种纸质版的，我想是吧。

728
00:34:39.190 --> 00:34:39.670
Why?
为什么？

729
00:34:39.910 --> 00:34:41.370
It's a waste of time.
那是在浪费时间。

730
00:34:41.630 --> 00:34:42.090
I don't know.
我不知道。

731
00:34:42.350 --> 00:34:43.790
It's a waste of stamps.
那是在浪费邮票。

732
00:34:43.790 --> 00:34:45.370
Because it was like etiquette back then.
因为那时候讲究礼节。

733
00:34:45.510 --> 00:34:45.770
I don't know.
我不知道。

734
00:34:45.770 --> 00:34:46.070
Back then.
那时候。

735
00:34:47.310 --> 00:34:48.810
Way back then.
很久以前了。

736
00:34:49.090 --> 00:34:50.430
No, but it's true.
不，但这是事实。

737
00:34:50.430 --> 00:34:52.290
I think there's a lot that has changed.
我觉得很多事情都已经变了。

738
00:34:52.490 --> 00:35:00.470
I remember getting in a huge argument with my mom about wedding planning because in her
我记得曾因为婚礼筹备和我妈大吵一架，因为在她那一代，

739
00:35:00.470 --> 00:35:06.750
generation, the bride planned the wedding with her parents because her parents paid for
新娘是和父母一起筹备婚礼的，因为婚礼是父母出钱，

740
00:35:06.750 --> 00:35:14.830
the wedding and it was like a party they threw for the bride and groom and I said, I want to
就像是他们为新郎新娘举办的一场派对，而我说，我想

741
00:35:14.830 --> 00:35:19.050
plan my wedding with my husband, the person who's going to be my husband.
和我的丈夫，也就是即将成为我丈夫的那个人一起筹备婚礼。

742
00:35:20.310 --> 00:35:29.030
Like my mom wanted to pick out our registry items with me and I was like, that feels so weird
比如我妈想和我一起去挑选结婚登记的礼品，我觉得这太奇怪了，

743
00:35:29.030 --> 00:35:33.430
to me that I would go with my mom to pick out my dishes.
我怎么会和我妈一起去挑餐具呢。

744
00:35:33.430 --> 00:35:38.670
Wouldn't I go with the person who's going to eat off the plates with me to pick them out?
难道不应该和那个以后要和我一起用这些盘子吃饭的人去挑吗？

745
00:35:38.850 --> 00:35:43.630
But there was like a generational divide in like how these things are done.
但在这些事情的处理方式上，确实存在代沟。

746
00:35:43.810 --> 00:35:47.890
And I feel like this is going to point to like another generational divide.
我觉得这也会指向另一种代沟。

747
00:35:47.890 --> 00:35:53.490
Like remember when you used to send these paper, save the date or even these paper wedding
就像记得以前你们会寄这种纸质的“预留日期”卡片，甚至纸质的婚礼

748
00:35:53.490 --> 00:35:54.090
invitations.
请柬吗。

749
00:35:54.830 --> 00:35:59.390
Nowadays, I get invited to weddings all the time where it's all online.
现在，我经常收到婚礼邀请，全都是在线的。

750
00:35:59.390 --> 00:36:05.510
I get an email and then I click on this website and the registry links are there and the RSVP
我收到一封邮件，然后点击那个网站，里面有礼品登记链接和回复邀请。

751
00:36:05.510 --> 00:36:08.870
is there and it's like all there and it's actually kind of awesome.
它就在那儿，一切都在那儿，而且其实还挺棒的。

752
00:36:09.150 --> 00:36:11.310
I like a lot of it that's online now.
我很喜欢现在网上有的很多东西。

753
00:36:11.310 --> 00:36:17.810
It makes it very easy to find information, but I still like getting a hand proper invitation.
它让查找信息变得非常容易，但我还是喜欢收到正式的纸质请柬。

754
00:36:17.850 --> 00:36:19.490
I don't need to save the date.
我不需要什么“预留日期”的提醒。

755
00:36:19.610 --> 00:36:21.930
I don't need a little card with directions.
我不需要那种带路线图的小卡片。

756
00:36:21.930 --> 00:36:26.790
I don't need a little special card that lets you know if I want to eat chicken or the pasta,
我也不需要那种让我选吃鸡肉还是意面的特殊小卡片，

757
00:36:26.790 --> 00:36:30.590
but I like getting the paper invitation.
但我就是喜欢收到纸质请柬。

758
00:36:30.930 --> 00:36:33.430
For some of my dearest friends, I've saved them.
对于我的一些挚友，我把请柬都留着呢。

759
00:36:33.570 --> 00:36:33.990
I don't know.
我也不知道。

760
00:36:34.070 --> 00:36:35.950
I also am a little bit of a pack rat, as we know.
而且如大家所知，我有点爱囤东西。

761
00:36:36.070 --> 00:36:36.830
I scrapbook.
我喜欢做剪贴簿。

762
00:36:37.110 --> 00:36:40.890
So I like getting the actual paper invitation myself.
所以我自己很喜欢收到真正的纸质请柬。

763
00:36:40.890 --> 00:36:42.390
I can be with you on that.
这点我能和你达成共识。

764
00:36:42.650 --> 00:36:47.070
I really like getting a paper thank you.
我真的很喜欢收到纸质的感谢信。

765
00:36:47.670 --> 00:36:48.110
Yeah.
没错。

766
